From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:57:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: rtkit-helper: Keep serving buffer requests on
 T8140 adopted sessions

Adopting a live session now refuses every buffer request, so that a
request cannot replace storage the firmware negotiated with the boot
stage. That is right when the producer published a buffer inventory, or
on T8132, where the input session is retained. The T8140 producer does
not publish one: its adopted MTP session used to map buffer requests
that point into the MTP SRAM, including the crashlog. They now fail, and
a J700 MTP crash is reported without its log.

Refuse new buffers only when the adopted session has an inventory or the
helper is the T8132 MTP. Other adopted sessions map SRAM IOVAs as before.

Fixes: 1fac0605f061 ("soc: apple: rtkit-helper: preserve the inherited J713 input session")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit fb96882f6cb4ce464fcf3f8b3f27f0c3eba891ed)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c
index c2f0d75f9a..6d958bfb00 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c
@@ -33,6 +33,11 @@ struct apple_rtkit_helper {
 	bool adopted;
 	/* The producer already began the J713 DockChannel input session. */
 	bool preserved;
+	/*
+	 * The adopted session has a buffer inventory: requests for buffers
+	 * it does not list must not replace storage the firmware still owns.
+	 */
+	bool strict_buffers;
 
 	void __iomem *asc_base;
 
@@ -63,7 +68,7 @@ static int apple_rtkit_helper_shmem_setup(void *cookie, struct apple_rtkit_shmem
 	 * allocation, or an unrecorded request from a legacy producer, does not
 	 * authorize replacing storage the firmware may still use.
 	 */
-	if (helper->adopted)
+	if (helper->adopted && helper->strict_buffers)
 		return -ENODATA;
 
 	if (!bfr->iova) {
@@ -309,8 +314,14 @@ static int apple_rtkit_helper_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	if (live) {
-		/* Set before RX starts: no new buffer allocation is safe here. */
+		/*
+		 * Set before RX starts: with an inventory, or on T8132, no new
+		 * buffer allocation is safe here. Producers that predate the
+		 * inventory (T8140) keep mapping IOVAs inside the SRAM region.
+		 */
 		helper->adopted = true;
+		helper->strict_buffers = count > 0 ||
+			of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-mtp");
 		helper->rtk = apple_rtkit_init_adopted_with_buffers(
 			dev, helper, NULL, 0, &apple_rtkit_helper_ops, buffers, count);
 		if (IS_ERR(helper->rtk))
